 "text": "Hey, good to have you here. How are you? Many laptops have an option in the keyboard settings to swap the right side keys so lefties can use them normally. Yes, it changes everything on the right to the left, so it takes a little getting used to. Look at laptops with a wide keyboard and long trackpad, and some come with a built-in keyboard cover with a full size layout. Some laptops have a split layer that flips in. Look for a full size layout, so the keys are spaced like a regular keyboard. Some companies even make lefty laptops.",
